   "source": [
    "The hourly utilization shows a very pronounced morning peak that dominates the entire daily pattern. During the night hours from 00:00 to 05:00, utilization is almost negligible, indicating that overnight demand at these stations is very small. Starting at around 06:00, utilization rises sharply until it reaches the maximum at 09:00, highlighted by the red dashed line in the chart.\n",
    "After the peak, utilization decreases at a gradual level until midnight. The absence of a second peak in the late afternoon or evening indicates that charging demand is much more strongly linked to the start of the day than to an evening return-home pattern.\n",
    "\n",
    "From an operational perspective, the interval from 08:00 to 11:00 can be seen as the critical window where demand regularly pushes closest to available capacity. If users experience queues or congestion, intervenitions such as adding more chargers, introducng time-limited parking or pricing incentives to shift some charging to other hours would be most efficient when targeted at this peak period."
   ]
  },
