    "## KPI 2: Energy delivered per Hour\n",
    "This KPI provides a detailed view of demand patterns, especially over the day and between the different sites. It reflects the total amount of energy that is actually delivered per hour, so it closely tracks real charging demand rather than just technical capacity. High hourly energy values indicate at which time and place demand regularly pushes the system closer to its limits. Conversely, low values show periods or sites with under-utilized capacity, where demand-shifting or consolidation might be possible.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Energy delivered}_{\\text{ hour h}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sum_{\\text{Sessions}}\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\text{Minutes}_{\\text{ session in hour h}}\n",
    "\\cdot\n",
    "\\frac{\\text{Energy delivered}_{\\text{ session}}}{\\text{Total minutes}_{\\text{ session}}}\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "$$"
   ]
